  ✕ Cannot write to `b.items[0]`
    ╭─[test.lis:10:3]
  9 │   let mut b = make()
 10 │   b.items[0] = 9
    ·   ───────┬──────
    ·          ╰── `b.items` is read-only
 11 │ }
    ╰────
  help: Declare the return type of `make` with `mut`, because `b` comes from it. `items` is declared writable, but `b` is read-only, so its fields are too · code: [infer.write_through_read_only]
